<title>USA: Northeast disciplines 22 at Millstone.</title>
<headline>Northeast disciplines 22 at Millstone.</headline>
<dateline>WATERFORD, Conn. 1997-07-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Northeast Utilities said Wednesday that that it has disciplined 22 employees for unacceptable performance while associated with the Millstone Training Department.</p>
<p>The company said that two-thirds of those involved held management or supervisory positions.</p>
<p>Northeast said that it took the actions following several critical audits, inspections and self-asessment at the nuclear power facility, which has been closed for the past 15 months.</p>
<p>It also said that the disciplinary actions, which included demotions, separations and suspensions without pay, were taken for past performance deficiencies and were not directly related to the Millstone training stand-down announced about three weeks ago.</p>
<p>All three units at the company's nuclear Millstone Station are awaiting approval from the Nuclear Regulatory Commission to restart, said the company.</p>
